{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>The drawer shell is for app-like products with persistent navigation —
     the Gmail-2020 pattern: a permanent inset nav column on wide screens,
     the same markup collapsing to an off-canvas drawer on phones.</p>
  <h3>Do use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your product has more destinations than a bottom bar can hold, and they
        deserve permanent visibility on desktop.</li>
    <li>You want one markup that is a nav column on desktop and a drawer on
        mobile, with no separate mobile template.</li>
    <li>The content is a feed/workspace (mail, docs, admin) rather than a flow.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The page is a marketing or landing page — no shell is needed.</li>
    <li>You only have 3–5 top-level destinations — the bottom-nav shell is
        simpler and more mobile-native.</li>
    <li>Navigation must stay visible while scrolling on phones; drawers are
        opened on demand there.</li>
  </ul>
  {{ callout({
